<article class="env-lemma" id="0587">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0587">Lemma <span data-tag="0587">10.63.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $M$ be an $R$-module. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  M = (0) \Leftrightarrow \text{Ass}(M) = \emptyset .  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $M = (0)$, then $\text{Ass}(M) = \emptyset $ by definition. If $M \not= 0$, pick any nonzero finitely generated submodule $M' \subset M$, for example a submodule generated by a single nonzero element. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0585" data-tag="0585">10.40.2</a> we see that $\text{Supp}(M')$ is nonempty. By Proposition <a href="/tag/02CE" data-tag="02CE">10.63.6</a> this implies that $\text{Ass}(M')$ is nonempty. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02M3" data-tag="02M3">10.63.3</a> this implies $\text{Ass}(M) \not= \emptyset $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>